  "version": "1.0",
  "changes_html": "<h2>About This Vintage</h2>\n<p>This is a historical reconstruction of The Budget Lab's \"State of U.S. Tariffs: October 30, 2025\" report, restructured to match the current interactive's data format. At the time of this release, the central open policy question was not Section 122 (which did not yet exist as a live issue) but whether the Supreme Court would invalidate the administration's use of the International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA) as legal authority for a large share of 2025 tariffs. The \"Baseline\" scenario below reflects tariff policy as it stood on October 30, 2025; the \"IEEPA Invalidation\" scenario models the counterfactual in which IEEPA-based tariffs are struck down and not replaced.</p>",
